Changes made on top of the shipped archive
------------------------------------------
The shipped archive is the authority for everything except the two import
fixes below, without which the package cannot be imported at all. Every
other byte of every operator module is identical to the archive.

  1. hybrid_moa_vl_operator_suite/__init__.py
     The shipped version imports `persistent_norm_sparse_topk_agg_kernel`
     from moa_triton_kernels, but that name is the *no-Triton stub*: it only
     exists when Triton is NOT installed. With Triton installed the real
     kernel is called `persistent_moa_norm_sparse_topk_megakernel`, so the
     import raised ImportError on any Triton-equipped machine (and the flat
     fallback then failed with ModuleNotFoundError). The import now resolves
     the real name first and falls back to the stub, exposing one stable
     public name either way.

  2. hybrid_moa_vl_operator_suite/unified_hybrid_moa_architecture.py
     The shipped version used bare module imports (`from moa_operators import
     ...`) guarded by a `sys.path.insert(0, _CURRENT_DIR)` hack. Loaded as a
     package that imports a *second* copy of every module under its bare name,
     so two copies of every class coexist and `isinstance` checks across them
     fail. Imports are now dual-mode: package-relative first, plain module
     path when the file is executed directly
     (`python3 unified_hybrid_moa_architecture.py`); the sys.path hack was
     removed.

